# Sphinx build output
_build/

# Generated doc assets — NOT checked in (kept separate from authored images,
# which live committed in another tree). Screenshots (per-block *-edit.png, the
# editor-guide shots, the mobile shots) and the demo video are regenerated into
# their served location by the screenshot specs / `pnpm demo:encode`, and in CI
# are cache-restored rather than recorded on every run (NSW-docs pattern).
# The mount SERVES them when present and only WARNS when absent (so a fresh
# checkout boots and can generate them); a final media-existence check runs
# after generation. The blob manifests (images/index.md, static/index.md) and
# all authored images stay committed.
images/*.png
static/hydra-demo.mp4

# Sphinx _static demo video (same rule, legacy path).
_static/hydra-demo.mp4
